      "writtenOn": "2026-01-26T15:18:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is overly strict for opaque, non-stencil draws so we should mention that exception.\n\nGiven what I found in https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1149956, it might make sense to track opaque+non-stencil binding lists separately from others, similarly to how the depth-only draws are separate. Then we could explicitly traverse first depth-only draws, then opaque draws (with binding lists doing their F2B ordering), then all the non-opaque draws (B2F)",
