        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-26T15:18:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It may be simpler to also use `fStorage` for holding the transforms. As we make progress, we can revisit that as well as the trivial destructibility of everything that we put in the arena. \n\nIf we can isolate all the arena objects to be things that don\u0027t require destructors, then we might benefit from having the non-trivial things pulled into separate collections where we don\u0027t have to skip around memory in the arena quite as much when it\u0027s reset.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "2bc1a63051b98202201826fe42b7454c5a01e4ac",
